>
> df<-data.frame(Lon=Lon, Lat=Lat, Value=Value)
> ggplot(df, aes(x=Lon, y=Lat))+geom_tile(aes(fill=Value))

geom_tile accepts a (mostly undocumented: appears only in the
examples) width aesthetic, so you can do e.g.,

ggplot(df, aes(x=Lon, y=Lat))+geom_tile(aes(fill=Value, width = .2))

If you want to get more complicated you could do something like

df <- df[order(df$Lon),]
df <- ddply(df, .(Lat), transform,
            lon.w = c(0, diff(Lon)))

ggplot(df, aes(x=Lon, y=Lat))+geom_tile(aes(fill=Value, width = lon.w))

but I haven't worked out how to deal with the fact that there is one
less value than there is width.

