It appears you need a reminder of the concept of a reproducible
example, since neither of your first two questions can really be
answered directly without one.
 http://gist.github.com/270442

I used the UCBAdmissions data set from the autoloaded datasets()
package, trying to adapt the core of your opts to the example (with
adjustments to make it look halfway presentable to me - e.g., dropping
the x-axis label).

u <- as.data.frame.table(UCBAdmissions)
ggplot(u, aes(x = Gender, y = Freq)) +
    theme_bw() +
    geom_bar(aes(fill = Admit), stat = 'identity') +
    facet_wrap(~ Dept) +
    scale_fill_manual(values = c('Admitted' = 'red',
                                 'Rejected' = 'skyblue')) +
    labs(x = '', y = 'Frequency', fill = 'Decision') +
    opts(legend.position="bottom",

         legend.direction="horizontal",
         legend.text = theme_text(colour="black",

                                   size = 14,
                                   face = "bold"),
         legend.title = theme_text(size = 20, face = 'bold'),
         panel.grid.major=theme_blank(),
         panel.grid.minor=theme_blank(),
         title="Admission status by gender/department",
         axis.text.y=theme_text(size=14, face="bold"),
         axis.text.x = theme_text(size = 14, face = 'bold'),
         axis.title.y = theme_text(size = 20, angle = 90, vjust = 0.2,
face = "bold"),
